Z||000000||Sweeet86GT||08-26-2001||12:25 PM||||my 86 gt has a busted EGR valve is disconnected at the valve.<BR>the vaccum line is plugged.<BR>i ran a diagnostic on the motor at the plug behind the cig liter and all i got was a 12 code.<BR>now you would think i would get another code.<BR>am i doing something wrong or not following enough steps.<P>------------------<BR>DAVE DIXON<BR>Bay City,MI||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||08-26-2001||12:49 PM||||I think the ECM will only pull an EGR code if the EGR control module goes. That's on the other end of the vacuum line. <BR>Otherwise, you'll probably pull an "O2- Too rich" (34?) after you let it idle for about 4-5 minutes. That's what mine did.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Joe Torma||08-26-2001||12:52 PM||||It flashed 12 more than 3 times right?<BR>If you have the solinoid line plugged, the solinoid may not know it isn't working.  Replace the valve and hook it back up.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sweeet86GT||08-26-2001||01:02 PM||||Yep<BR>it flashed 12 until i pulled the jumper.<BR>i did let it run for awhile before i tried the test.what would happen if i just left it unplugged and not working?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||08-26-2001||02:08 PM||||Well, it is supposed to give you higher emissions and cause your car to detonate.  Use 93 octane.  Romp on it...does it ping?<BR>||||reg||1
